    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-062: `linear-gradient()` background support**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~280-350 lines, 5 files) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\nCloses the last 1/11 `background:` form that Wikipedia CSS uses. Full grammar coverage achieved (11/11 forms parse).\n\n**Honest framing: zero Wikipedia delta expected.** The Wikipedia gradient target is triple-blocked (see below). This ADR is **synthetic-fixture verified only** — same class as ADR-054's rotate.\n\n## The triple-blocked Wikipedia target\n\nThe only `linear-gradient` in Wikipedia's CSS is:\n\n```css\n.vector-sticky-pinned-container::after {\n    background: linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0),\n                                var(--background-color-base,#fff));\n    position: sticky;\n    ...\n}\n```\n\n**Three independent blockers make it invisible regardless of ADR-062:**\n\n| Layer | Status | Blocking ADR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` ancestor | `h=0` (culled) | ADR-050 diagnostic; separate culling ADR |\n| `::after` pseudo-element | Synthesized (ADR-041) but parent `h=0` | Nothing to see |\n| `position: sticky` | Deferred | Separate scroll-aware layout ADR |\n\n**The CSS parser gap is real** (1/11 forms dropped entirely), the **paint infrastructure is reusable** (future gradients on buttons, headers, dialogs), and **the grammar is now complete** — but the current Wikipedia target remains culled.\n\n## What ships\n\n### Parser (`stylesheet.cpp`)\n\nReplace the blanket `if (gradient( in value) return false;` (line 617) with a targeted `linear-gradient(...)` extraction branch. Preserves the raw gradient string as `background-image: linear-gradient(...)`. Nested parens respected (for `var()` / `rgba()` inside stops). Stray commas outside the gradient still drop (multi-layer deferral).\n\n### Data model (`layout_box.hpp`)\n\nNew struct + fields:\n```cpp\nstruct BackgroundGradientStop {\n    Color color;\n    float position;  // 0.0 .. 1.0\n};\nbool background_is_gradient = false;\nfloat background_gradient_angle_deg = 180.0f;  // default\nstd::vector<BackgroundGradientStop> background_gradient_stops;\n```\n\n### Layout (`layout.cpp`)\n\n`parse_background_gradient` helper (~60 lines): splits on top-level commas, parses optional direction (`Ndeg` or `to <keyword>` incl. corners), then stop colors via existing `parse_color`. Angle default 180deg (top→bottom).\n\n### Paint (`paint.cpp`)\n\n`paint_background_gradient` (~50 lines): computes gradient line endpoints from angle + half-diagonal (`hl = (w*|cos| + h*|sin|)/2`, per CSS spec §3.1.1), then Cairo linear pattern with per-stop `add_color_stop_rgba`. Fills box rect.\n\nCall site in `paint_box` — gradient first (fill), then URL image if present (layered).\n\n## Grammar coverage\n\n| Form | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `linear-gradient(red, blue)` (default 180deg) | ✅ |\n| `linear-gradient(45deg, red, blue)` | ✅ |\n| `linear-gradient(to bottom/right/left/top, ...)` | ✅ |\n| `linear-gradient(to bottom right, ...)` (corner) | ✅ |\n| 3+ stops | ✅ |\n| Wikipedia's `rgba(255,255,255,0) → white` | ✅ |\n| **Stop positions** (`red 20%`) | ⚠️ Parsed, treated as uniform |\n| `radial-gradient` / `conic-gradient` | ❌ Dropped |\n| Multi-layer (`url(x), linear-gradient(...)`) | ❌ Dropped |\n| `in oklab` interpolation | ❌ Dropped |\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**Structured parse in layout, not css:** `css/` cannot include `layout::parse_color` (layering, ADR-055). css parser preserves raw string; layout resolves structured form where `parse_color` + `LengthContext` are available.\n\n**Separate `paint_background_gradient`:** different Cairo primitives (linear pattern vs surface), different lifecycle. Merging would add type dispatch to the hot image path.\n\n**Include `to <corner>` forms:** 8-line switch, no cost, useful for future real pages.\n\n**Stop positions parsed but ignored in v1:** Wikipedia uses defaults `0% / 100%` — unaffected. Real gradient-with-positions needs ~60-line position-fill algorithm; follow-up ADR.\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- **Zero Wikipedia delta.** Target triple-blocked (see Context).\n- **No visible production change.**\n- **Stop positions uniform**, not `%`-exact.\n- **No radial / conic / repeating.**\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Synthetic-fixture-verified.** 5-row fixture at `docs/adr062-gradient-test.html`:\n- Solid color control\n- Default vertical gradient\n- 45° diagonal gradient\n- 3-stop horizontal\n- Wikipedia's exact `rgba(255,255,255,0) → white`\n\n**Wikipedia screenshot: unchanged** — parser-only for existing content, gradient target remains culled.\n\n## Test count target\n\n- 683 → ~689 (+6 tests)\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Stop positions (`red 20%` — parsed, uniform interpolation applied)\n- Radial / conic / repeating gradients\n- Multi-layer gradients\n- Color interpolation spaces\n- Gradient rendering inside `::before` / `::after` on visible parents\n- `position: sticky` (the target's third blocker)\n\nRefs #264\n",
